{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1111","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1111","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1111\",\"parent_revision\":\"e0436087739477d28639ced5cab56ef8af1a02f0\",\"root_revision\":\"c5bbb80f3943dfdfb2c402b8d218c4886cf75677bf184c50ada7013c9af5006b\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAssessment date: 2026-04-23\\n\\n| # | Condition | Status | Source |\\n|---|-----------|--------|--------|\\n| 1 | Vocabulary canary list (terms to monitor) | DERIVABLE | Extract from CLAUDE.md constraint sections |\\n| 2 | Hook event for post-compression detection | MISSING | Claude Code compression events may not be hookable |\\n| 3 | Output type classification (when to check vs not) | MISSING | Must be designed |\\n| 4 | Claude Code compression event API | MISSING | Research required \u2014 unknown if post-compression hooks exist |\\n\\nVerdict: BLOCKED \u2014 fundamental feasibility question: does Claude Code expose a post-compression hook event? If not, the approach must change (e.g., periodic scan hook). Research required before architecture is defined.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **vocabulary canary list for constraint persistence after compression** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Research entry: ./research/ai-observability/compression-monitor.md -- pattern: Ghost Lexicon vocabulary decay detection\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-29\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Impact\\n\\nP1 Feature. Depends on Claude Code hook API research. Architecture blocked pending feasibility verification.\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- A canary list of constraint vocabulary terms is defined (e.g., 'reproduction-first', 'fail-fast', 'chain of verification', 'stateless handoff', 'surgical removal')\\n- A hook or check runs after compression events and scans recent agent output for canary terms\\n- When canary terms are absent from outputs that should contain them (e.g., a fix-related output missing 'reproduction-first'), an alert is emitted\\n- Alert format: 'CANARY MISSING: {term} not found in last N outputs \u2014 compression may have dropped constraint context'\\n- The canary list is defined in `.claude/rules/vocabulary-canary.md` or equivalent\\n- False positive rate is low: canary checks only activate on output types where the term is expected (fix outputs, delegation outputs, not casual conversation)\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `.claude/rules/vocabulary-canary.md` \u2014 canary term list (new file)\\n- `.claude/hooks/` \u2014 canary check hook (type TBD pending compression event research)\\n- `.claude/hooks/hooks.json` \u2014 register hook\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an agent operating after context compression, I need a vocabulary canary list that verifies whether high-precision constraint terms from CLAUDE.md still appear in my outputs so silent behavioral drift from compression is detectable.\\n\\n## Target State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nA vocabulary canary list is maintained as a structured file at `.claude/rules/vocabulary-canary.md` containing high-precision constraint terms extracted from CLAUDE.md and rules/. A companion script `vocabulary_canary_check.py` takes a session JSONL log and checks whether canary terms appear in orchestrator outputs before and after detected compression boundaries. A decay score above 0.3 triggers a warning.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Measurable Signal\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nFile `.claude/rules/vocabulary-canary.md` exists with 20+ high-precision terms. Running `vocabulary_canary_check.py --session {path}` produces a decay score and lists ghost terms (present pre-compression, absent post-compression). Score below 0.1 = LOW, 0.1-0.3 = MODERATE, above 0.3 = HIGH.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Current State\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nCLAUDE.md and .claude/rules/ define high-precision constraint terms (e.g., \\\"surgical removal\\\", \\\"fail-fast\\\", \\\"reproduction-first\\\", \\\"chain of verification\\\", \\\"stateless handoff\\\") that agents must follow. After context compression, there is no mechanism to verify whether the orchestrator's outputs still contain these terms. If compression causes the orchestrator to stop using \\\"reproduction-first\\\" vocabulary while still producing fix-related outputs, the behavioral change is invisible.\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"150868951cf3695f7ef948374f8898df62244918d0c3c295ef6cb83a2da1004c\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPt4lEA\"}"}